{
  "id": "place-sharpen",
  "title": "Equal-extent Place sharpens with adaptive contrast and exact zero",
  "binding": "The shipped Place kernel reads a 16x48 seed at equal extent. The softened edge uses exact codes64,96,160,192. At x7 the four-neighbor average is104 and normalized contrast is0.6, so sharpness1 gives96+(96-104)/1.6=91; at x8 it gives160+8/1.5=165.333, encoded165. Strength0.4 gives94 exactly, avoiding a half-code conversion tie. Flat colors and the black/white hard edge stay exact. The control applies sharpness1 to the nominal copy capture, so the zero-strength copy observation fails. This uses the existing Place dispatch and writes the same768 output texels at every strength.",
  "bootShape": "offscreen",
  "backends": [
    "vulkan",
    "directx"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "gpu"
  ],
  "timeoutSeconds": 60,
